# LAMMPS input for backmapping — generated by backmap-prep, hand-tuned
# 3-phase protocol (see rim135_diag/in.rim135_v2, 2026-07-12 VM regression).
# Reference: Krajniak et al., JCTC 2016, DOI: 10.1021/acs.jctc.6b00595
#            Krajniak, Zhang et al., JCC 2018, DOI: 10.1002/jcc.25129
#
# Data/table inputs (rim135.data, table_*.table, pairs.dat) are generated by
# `backmap-prep build-hybrid examples/epoxy/settings.v2.yaml` from bakery's
# rim135 reference data (see ../README.md) and are intentionally not
# committed here (large, regenerable). Run this script from a directory that
# has those files alongside it.
#
# Protocol notes (fixes the catastrophic divergence seen under the
# corrected global-lambda weighting model, notebook
# 2026-07-12_lambda-weighting-vm-regression.md):
#   Phase 0a — minimize with CG frozen (removes AT/AT overlaps from rigid
#              fragment placement before any dynamics).
#   Phase 0b — gentle AT relaxation (CG still frozen), tiny dt (0.01 fs),
#              nve/limit, no thermostat needed since KE stays bounded.
#   Phase 1  — lambda ramp (dt 0.10 fs), nve/limit + Langevin thermostat on
#              AT atoms throughout, matching the original AdResS protocol's
#              always-on damping (Krajniak et al. JCTC 2016). Without the
#              thermostat, the new model's "instant full-strength AT
#              same-bead" onset spikes T to ~1e7 K within a few thousand
#              steps; with it, T recovers to ~300 K by lambda=0.5.
#   Phase 2  — NVT production with a gradual dt ramp-up (0.25 -> 0.50 -> 1.00 fs).

units real
atom_style full
boundary p p p

read_data rim135.data

reset_atoms image all

comm_modify cutoff 82.23

pair_style backmap 12.00 lj/cut/coul/cut 12.00 9.00 14.00 table linear 1000
